WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.369
Part eleven: My return at a CA firm, for an H U F and for a consultant. Pick a person - or start from a document.

2
00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:23.279
No client to add first. The family H U F's pre-filled JSON goes in, and the H U F is made from it - its P A N, name and the day it was formed.

3
00:00:23.891 --> 00:00:36.371
Deposit interest and the tax the bank deducted, read. An H U F never files I T R 1 and gets no 87 A rebate: its form is I T R 2.

4
00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:43.279
The return of an H U F is signed by its Karta: his name and P A N go here.

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.539
Both regimes for the H U F, the cheaper one marked.

6
00:00:53.141 --> 00:01:04.781
Next, Kavya: a consultant with no Form 16 - fees from her clients, with tax deducted under 194 J. Her pre-filled JSON makes her too.

7
00:01:05.407 --> 00:01:14.627
Her bank statement: fifteen lakh ninety thousand of receipts, sixty thousand in cash - interest and her own transfers kept apart.

8
00:01:18.641 --> 00:01:29.821
She is registered for G S T, so her G S T R 3 B summary goes in too: the turnover for each G S T I N, the months added up.

9
00:01:30.438 --> 00:01:40.468
On review, her work: a profession under 44 A D A. One click takes the receipts from the bank statement, and half of them is her income.

10
00:01:41.078 --> 00:01:59.198
The G S T schedule: her G S T I N and its turnover, read from the G S T R 3 B - and set beside the receipts in the return. Sixteen and a half lakh both ways: they agree. Another G S T I N is one more line.

11
00:01:59.813 --> 00:02:08.283
Her nature of work, and her father's name for the return. The form follows: I T R 4, Sugam.

12
00:02:08.891 --> 00:02:17.481
If she keeps her own accounts instead - her gross profit and expenses typed, the profit worked out - it is I T R 3.

13
00:02:20.828 --> 00:02:36.068
With her own accounts, two more figures: all she paid out in the year, and how much of it in cash. Cash under five percent on both sides, so the tax-audit limit for a profession is seventy-five lakh, not fifty.

14
00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:53.778
Had she run a shop instead - a business - one more question: did she leave 44 A D in the last five years? Then 44 A D stays closed to her for five years, and income above the exemption needs a tax audit: a CA's return.

15
00:02:54.391 --> 00:03:01.061
File: I T R 3, made from My return and checked against the department's schema.

16
00:03:01.672 --> 00:03:06.302
Last, part twelve: the tax rules themselves.
